This crate (`symphonia-codec-amrwb`) is a pure-Rust AMR-WB (Adaptive Multi-Rate Wideband, ITU-T
G.722.2) speech decoder. It is licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of
Project Symphonia.

The algorithm is specified by 3GPP TS 26.190 / 26.173 / 26.201 (ITU-T G.722.2). This implementation
follows the structure of FFmpeg's AMR-WB decoder: `libavcodec/amrwbdec.c`, `amrwbdata.h` and the
shared CELP code it uses (`lsp.c`, `celp_filters.c`, `celp_math.c`, `acelp_filters.c`,
`acelp_vectors.c`, `acelp_pitch_delay.c`). The codebook, ISF, window and bit-reordering tables in
`src/tables.rs` were taken from those files. FFmpeg is distributed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 2.1 or later.

